{{/*
   Target paths listed here are NOT applied on this machine. Evaluated per
   machine against the data in ~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml, so one branch
   serves every host.

   Everything not listed is applied everywhere: configs for tools that are not
   installed (fish, tofi, wofi, sioyek, spotify ...) are inert, and land ready
   for the machine that does have them.

   Only two kinds of thing are listed below. Mutually exclusive choices, where
   applying both would be ambiguous rather than harmless -- the window-manager
   trees and their portal configs. And retired configs kept as reference, which
   are switched off on every host rather than per-host.

   mako is deliberately in neither list: it is the notification daemon on every
   host now that sway has moved off swaync, so it applies everywhere.
*/ -}}
{{ if ne .wm "mango"    }}.config/mango{{ end }}
{{ if ne .wm "hyprland" }}.config/hypr{{ end }}
{{ if ne .wm "sway"     }}.config/sway{{ end }}

{{/*
   xdg-desktop-portal reads $XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP-portals.conf, and each
   compositor sets a different value: mango -> wlroots, hyprland -> Hyprland,
   sway -> sway. Only the matching one is installed.
*/ -}}
{{ if ne .wm "mango"    }}.config/xdg-desktop-portal/wlroots-portals.conf{{ end }}
{{ if ne .wm "hyprland" }}.config/xdg-desktop-portal/hyprland-portals.conf{{ end }}
{{ if ne .wm "sway"     }}.config/xdg-desktop-portal/sway-portals.conf{{ end }}

{{/*
   Tracked as reference, deliberately never linked on any host. The configs stay
   in the repo -- they are finished work and cost nothing to keep -- but nothing
   reads them, so applying them would just leave dead files in ~/.config.

     ncmpcpp  superseded by rmpc, which is the mpd client on every host now.
     aerc     retired; the account config is kept for whenever mail comes back.
     sioyek   zathura is the document reader on every host.
     spotify  the spicetify theme outlived the account.
     clipse   retired on every host; it was a `go install` binary, never a
              package, so it is not in the deps script either.
     wlogout  not used on mango or sway; neither host has a power menu.
     wofi     tofi is the launcher on sway, walker on mango.

   Unconditional, not switched on .wm: none of these is host-specific.
*/ -}}
.config/ncmpcpp
.config/aerc
.config/sioyek
.config/spotify
.config/clipse
.config/wlogout
.config/wofi
